---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
import PhotoHero from "@dst/ui/district/PhotoHero.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
import { siteHeaderImage, currentPhase, soldOutPhase, currentUnits } from "../content";
---
<Layout
  title="Payment Plan"
  description="Palm Central's payment plan — what's confirmed for the sold-out Phase 1, what's reported but unconfirmed for the current Phase 2, and what to get in writing before booking."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <PhotoHero
      eyebrow="Payment plan"
      title="What the payment plan actually is"
      image={siteHeaderImage.src}
      imageAlt={siteHeaderImage.alt}
    />
    <p class="lede">
      Nakheel's own release for {currentPhase.label} doesn't publish exact
      payment terms. A few brokers list specific percentages anyway —
      treat those as estimates until your sales contact confirms them in
      writing, not as the developer's stated plan.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>{soldOutPhase.label} — confirmed structure (sold out)</h2>
    <p>
      The sold-out first phase used a documented 20/50/30 structure:
    </p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>20% at booking</strong> — due on reservation.</li>
      <li><strong>50% during construction</strong> — split across roughly seven to eight milestone installments.</li>
      <li><strong>30% on handover</strong> — due {soldOutPhase.handover}.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      On the AED 2.5M entry price, that put the booking amount at
      <strong>AED 500,000</strong> — the number that made this phase's
      1-bedroom units accessible relative to the total price.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="warn">
    <strong>{currentPhase.label} terms aren't officially published.</strong> Several
    broker sites describe a similar 20% booking / staged construction
    payments / 30% handover plan for the current phase, with construction
    installments reportedly running from late 2026 through early 2029 —
    but this comes from secondary sources, not Nakheel's own release. Get
    the actual schedule from your sales contact before you book on the
    strength of a number you read on a listing site.
  </Callout>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What to ask for before booking</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The exact installment schedule with dates, not just percentages — construction-linked payments can move if the build timeline shifts.</li>
      <li>Whether the plan differs by unit type. On Phase 1, larger units and townhouses reportedly ran a different split than 1–2 bedroom apartments; confirm whether that still applies.</li>
      <li>What happens to your payments if handover slips past {currentPhase.handover} — Nakheel has a strong delivery record, but the contract terms are what actually govern this, not the track record.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="container cta">
    <h2>Want the current schedule?</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="#interest" title="Register interest in Palm Central">Register your interest</a> and
      we'll come back with the actual payment schedule for the unit type
      you're looking at, confirmed rather than estimated.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm currentUnits={currentUnits} />
</Layout>

<style>
  .steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .steps li { max-width: 65ch; }
  .cta { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
